superv for Debian
-----------------

SuperV registers its keyboard shortcuts (Super+V and any extras you turn on) in
your desktop's own settings. Package removal doesn't touch your personal
settings, so to give the desktop its shortcuts back, run this as your user
before removing the package:

    superv --remove-hotkeys

Pasting into other applications uses a virtual keyboard (/dev/uinput). The
package's udev rule lets the user at the active seat use it, the same rule
steam-devices ships; it is write-only, so SuperV can press keys but never read
them.

 -- Saikat Roy <saikathub95@gmail.com>
